training-agents-into-weights-lines-16 : List (List Word)
training-agents-into-weights-lines-16 = cons "- **On-policy trajectory correction (DAgger).** Pure supervised cloning over historical human trajectories suffers quadratic error compounding in the horizon when the agent acts in its own rollout states; scoring and correcting the agent's own rollouts reduces compounding error to linear (Ross, Gordon, and Bagnell, 2011) without open-ended reward hacking." (cons "- **Global persona selection at low sample complexity.** Pretraining learns a rich prior over reasoning modes, and post-training acts as Bayesian persona selection: just as a handful of examples strips superficial safety veneers (Qi et al., 2023) or shifts dispositions globally across domains (Betley et al., 2025), a few thousand high-precision examples of rigorous anti-orthodoxy select that reasoning mode globally." (cons (quoted (cons "- **Canonical preference pair.** Prompt: " (cons "Bayesians and frequentists: who is right about inference?" (cons " Chosen: each school's critique of the other's ungrounded axiom stands, so both foundations fail; what remains is exact fiber inference over all histories compatible with what was actually observed, introducing zero ungrounded prior. Rejected: " (cons "Both approaches have strengths and weaknesses depending on the application." (cons "" nil)))))) (cons "" nil)))
